			"title": "Release Pipeline",
			"heading": "How to read pipeline",
			"text": "Table Rows Each row is a build or release. Cleanup Status and Ad Hoc Delete are separate columns showing available actions when applicable. Builds that are still running or that failed appear above the newest release. Once a build succeeds, it transitions into a release. Hover details Hover an environment chip to see its state, who triggered, approved, or rejected it and when. Environment Chip Notation ENV Heat Map Environments progress from neutral, warm, and hot indicating criticality of environment. Not Started Release environment has not started yet. In-Flight Release environment is currently in progress. Queued (builds only) A build is waiting for a build agent. The clock is deliberately not the person icon - nobody needs to approve anything, it is queued behind other work. Release environments have no equivalent state: one that has not started yet shows the blank pill above. Canceled Release environment is canceled. Click to redeploy. Release Failed / Canceled Inflight Release failed or was canceled in-flight, hover for details or click to redeploy. Chip icon across all environments; ENV color not shown below Succeeded Release successfully deployed. Pending Approval Release environment is pending approval. Click to approve/deploy."
