			"text": "By default, sites already have a filter expression defined that includes known CalcEngines at time of latest release. You can modify the expression filter in the 'CalcEngine Filter' input in the header bar's filter row. Expression Rules Filter expressions are comma-separated and use OR logic when multiple expressions are provided. A plain value simply matches an exact CalcEngine name. See first example below. Instead of a plain value, the following commands are available: StartsWith:pattern, EndsWith:pattern, or Contains:pattern. See second example below. Chain commands within a single expression with ! for AND NOT logic. See third example below. To make a chained command be simply AND logic, prefix a later command with ^. See fourth example below. Filter Result Conduent_Nexgen_SAMPLE_BRD_SE.xlsm Matches exact name of a CalcEngine. StartsWith:Conduent_Nexgen_ Names beginning with that prefix. StartsWith:Conduent_Nexgen_!EndsWith:BRD_SE Starts with the prefix but does not end with BRD_SE. StartsWith:Conduent_Nexgen_!^Contains:_BRD_SE. Starts with the prefix and contains _BRD_SE."
