			"anchor": "app-refresh",
			"title": "Keyboard Shortcuts",
			"heading": "Application refresh shortcuts",
			"text": "The refreshes you reach for most often have keys. F5 is the app bar's whole-site Refresh. The others each do exactly what that section's ↻ button does: re-fetch that section and leave every other card alone. F5 Refreshes the whole site, the same as the app bar's Refresh. Ctrl+Shift+W Re-runs every saved Work Items query: the chips and the results of whichever queries are open. Ctrl+Shift+Q Re-runs just the open query, the same as the ↻ at the end of its results' action bar. With no query's results open, it does nothing. Ctrl+Shift+R Refreshes the Release Pipeline, the Release Pipeline KPI tile, and Release Differences together, because all three come from one fetch. Ctrl+Shift+C Refreshes the CalcEngine Pipeline. On a site with no CalcEngine filter there is no card to refresh, so the key does nothing."
