			"text": "The bar across the top of the window has access keys for its site picker, its Refresh and its filter boxes. Press and release Alt on its own to underline their letters; press it again, or click anywhere, to hide them. Like the refresh shortcuts, they are ignored while a dialog is open - a dialog uses Alt for its own fields. Alt+S Opens the site picker with its search box focused. Type to narrow the list, ↑/↓ (or Page Up/Page Down) to move, Enter to load the highlighted site and Esc to close it without changing anything. With the closed picker focused, typing a letter opens it with that letter already searched. Alt+R Refresh, the same as F5. Alt+F / Alt+T / Alt+C Focus From Release #, To Release # or CalcEngine Filter, showing the filter row first if it was hidden. Enter In a release box, refreshes the Release Pipeline with the new numbers; in CalcEngine Filter, refreshes the CalcEngine Pipeline. Nothing else is re-fetched."
