			"text": "With a query open, the grid can be driven from the keyboard without reaching for the mouse. The keys match GitHub's, so they should already be in your fingers. They also work when focus is on one of the app bar's buttons - after clicking Refresh, for instance - so you do not have to click back into the grid first. The exception is when you are typing in a box, such as the site search or a filter box, where a letter means what it always means. Navigation j Move down one row, wrapping from the last row back to the first. With nothing selected yet, selects the first row. k Move up one row, wrapping from the first row round to the last. With nothing selected yet, selects the last row. o Open the selected row's work item detail - the same thing clicking its title does. Does nothing when no row is selected. Esc Unselects the currently selected row. Actions - Grid focused All actions open 'edit' dialog for a task's Assigned To, Comment, State and Triage. These same actions are also available on each row's Context Menu. c Add Comment to the selected row. Defaults: Comment = Default Comment Text. r Return Task to previous owner. Defaults: Triage = Pending, Reassign To = previous owner, Comment = Default Return Task Comment. t Triage Task. Defaults: Triage = Triaged, Comment = Default Triage Comment. x Close Task. Defaults: State = Closed, Comment = Default Close Task Comment. Return Triaged Tasks Space Tick or untick the selected row's checkbox while a batch workflow is active."
