			"text": "The profile button \uE77B at the right of the app bar opens Settings. Hover it to see who you are signed in as for each account. It combines multiple setting management functions into a single, cohesive dialog. Your passwords and token are never shown back to you. Their boxes stay empty, and an empty box means \"keep what is saved\". Settings follows the app's theme and fits the window and shrinks from its full size in a smaller window when necessary. Profile holds your KAT DataStore, Conduent and TFS sign-ins. Display lets you choose separate palettes for Light and Dark modes, select Light, Dark or System color mode, and switch between Normal and Compact density. Work Items holds the settings that drive the functionality of viewing and managing work items. Queries are now added, edited and removed here rather than on the Work Items card: Add or Edit slides the query's settings over the page, a changed query shows a dot and an Undo, and nothing is saved until you press Save. See Creating Queries Views. Connections controls how the application connects to external services, including automatic updates, api polling, and online documentation."
