			"heading": "Work Item Detail reads like a document and a conversation",
			"text": "Work Item Detail used to be two collapsible boxes you had to open before you could read anything. It is now the thing you actually came for: the description as prose at a comfortable measure, and the discussion underneath it as a single threaded conversation. Comments carry the author's initials in a colored circle, and a person keeps the same color everywhere and between sessions, so you learn a thread's cast at a glance. A rail connects one comment to the next so a six-message back-and-forth reads as one exchange rather than six disconnected rows. The summary line above the thread is also the controls. Click a person's initials to show only their comments and everyone else dims out; click again for everyone. Newest and Oldest flip the order, and the count re-reads itself for whatever is in view. A long description is trimmed to about four lines and fades out, with Show full description to open it - and the fade only appears once there is genuinely more to show, so a two-line description never looks truncated. Comment bodies keep their formatting instead of flattening it. Code blocks, inline code, lists, bold and links all render, and a pasted screenshot is a real image you can click to enlarge rather than a broken box. Times read as 2 hours ago or Yesterday, with the exact timestamp on hover. See Work Item Detail."
