			"title": "Version 1.3",
			"heading": "Improvements",
			"text": "A new Keyboard Shortcuts page in Help lists every shortcut in one place. The application bar is part of the application. It stays in place as you scroll, follows the theme, and grows with everything else when you zoom with Ctrl+mouse wheel. In a narrow window the bar wraps onto two lines, Refresh shrinks to a ↻ icon and the filter button joins the icons on the right. Errors and warnings now appear in a themed bar along the bottom of the window. A warning and an error can show at the same time, each with its own × to dismiss it, and a long message scrolls instead of taking over the window. The bar stays visible even while a dialog is open, without covering the dialog's buttons. Each section's ↻ refresh button now shows its keyboard shortcut in its tooltip, for example \"(Ctrl+Shift+R)\" to refresh the Release Pipeline. Unsaved edits in Add Comment, Triage, Return Task, Close Task and Create New are protected by Discard your changes?. In comment dialogs, Esc prompts only after a user edit; Cancel closes directly. While the dashboard loads, the new loading screen shows what is happening to get KCC up and running. Keys and right-click that behave like an app. 'Browser-like' behavior is minimized giving KCC a more native application feel. Hold Ctrl while you right-click to get the browser's menu anywhere (or F12), for troubleshooting. The Work Items card is simpler: the add query button and each query's edit and delete buttons are gone, now that queries are managed in Settings. The bar reads Work Items, its ?, then Task ID Search, Search and Create New. A query can now Hide chip when no work items present, so a query with nothing in it stops taking room on the bar. It is on for new queries; queries you already have keep their chips until you turn it on in Settings. Ctrl+Shift+Q re-runs just the query whose results are open, the same as the ↻ at the end of its action bar. A query's filter box names the query it filters, for example \"Filter My To Do's items…\". Work Item Detail always shows Details and Links in a stable tab strip. A tab with no content is dimmed and unavailable; Links collects related work items, associated commits and builds. The batch return flow is consistently named Return Triage Tasks in its action and dialog. The Diagnostics trace now has a bounded scroll area, with jumps to the first entry, the first unseen entry and the newest entry. Release Differences lets you collapse commits by repository or hide a whole release group while keeping its headers fixed during scrolling. CalcEngine Pipeline's download action now uses a download arrow instead of a save icon. Copying a work-item ID includes its # prefix, and Task ID Search accepts that prefix when pasted. Conduent links show an orange border on hover. The footer's product and generated text is gone; zoom guidance now sits in the header before Last Refresh. The production-release check for the site-picker dot is configurable in Settings, with a 20-minute default."
